},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ralph Babet","party":"United Australia Party","person_id":"tvfy_11003","person_slug":"ralph-babet","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Dowling","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11056","person_slug":"richard-dowling","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steph Hodgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tyron Whitten","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_11060","person_slug":"tyron-whitten","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Defence Housing Australia Amendment Bill 2025 - Third Reading - Pass the bill","noes":11,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2025-08-25.239.1) to pass the bill in the Senate. In parliamentary jargon, they voted to read the bill a third time. Since the bill has already passed in the House of the Representatives, it will now become law. ### What does this bill do? According to the [bills digest](https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/bd/bd2526/26bd007), which is a document created by the parliamentary library: > *Australia is hosting an increasing number of foreign military personnel as a result of expanding defence cooperation with allies.* > > *Key initiatives include Submarine Rotational Force-West (SRF-West), the US Force Posture Initiatives, the Australia-Japan Reciprocal Access Agreement, and the Australia – Singapore Military Training Initiative.* > > *The Bill will amend the Defence Housing Australia Act 1987 to expand Defence Housing Australia’s (DHA) main function to include the ability to provide housing and housing-related services to foreign government and defence personnel, and philanthropic organisations assisting the Australian Defence Force, to meet Defence’s current and future operational requirements.* > > *At the time of writing, the Bill had not been referred to or reported on by any parliamentary committees.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-9696","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2025-08-25/14"}
